From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:04:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): no cursor in an unfocused ghostty pane

Cascadia draws no cursor at all when a pane loses focus; ghostty's default -
like most terminals - is a hollow block. Side by side that did not read as a
different convention, it read as the cursor setting being ignored, because every
shape collapsed to the same hollow box the moment focus moved.

cursor-style-unfocused = hidden (ghostty patch 30) asks for cascadia's
behaviour. Nothing about the focused cursor changes.

WT suites: unitControl 62/62.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp         | 6 ++++++
 src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp   | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
index f17f9769d..4d04dfe8b 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
@@ -142,6 +142,12 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
             }
         }
 
+        // Cascadia draws no cursor at all in an unfocused pane; ghostty's
+        // default - like most terminals - is a hollow block, so every shape
+        // became the same hollow box the moment focus moved. Next to a cascadia
+        // pane that is simply wrong rather than merely different.
+        set("cursor-style-unfocused", "hidden");
+
         // --- Padding ------------------------------------------------------
         // WT already insets the SwapChainPanel by this same padding, so asking
         // ghostty to pad as well would double it. Ours is therefore zero, and
diff --git a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
index cd44a051d..73ad2b208 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
@@ -220,6 +220,14 @@ namespace ControlUnitTests
                                        til::u8u16(c.expected))
                                .c_str());
         }
+
+        // Whatever the shape, an unfocused pane shows no cursor - cascadia
+        // draws none, where ghostty's default is a hollow block. Without this
+        // every shape collapsed to the same hollow box the moment focus moved,
+        // which reads as the cursor setting being ignored.
+        VERIFY_IS_TRUE(_has(Control::implementation::TranslateGhosttySettings(*_settings()),
+                            "cursor-style-unfocused",
+                            "hidden"));
     }
 
     // The one escaping rule left, and it belongs to the field rather than to
